  "description": "Construct a 0-indexed m x n matrix representing the structure of a binary tree.",
  "target": null,
  "pseudocode": "1. height = getHeight(root)\n2. width = 2^(height + 1) - 1\n3. res = new Array(height).fill(null).map(() => new Array(width).fill(''))\n4. fill(root, 0, 0, width - 1, res)\n5. function fill(node, depth, left, right, res):\n6.   mid = (left + right) / 2\n7.   res[depth][mid] = node.val\n8.   if node.left: fill(node.left, depth + 1, left, mid - 1, res)\n9.   if node.right: fill(node.right, depth + 1, mid + 1, right, res)",
